{"id": "section-body-03192", "title": "Anthrax", "chapterId": "chapter-four", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "NOTIFIABLE DISEASES", "Bacterial Infections", "Anthrax"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-03192", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Anthrax", "runs": [{"text": "Anthrax"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1802"}}, {"id": "body-03193", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Anthrax is a bacterial disease caused by the spore forming Bacillus anthraces, a gram positive, rod- shaped bacterium. It is a zoonotic disease whereby man is infected directly through contact with infected hides or inhalation of spores in the lungs or ingestion of infected meat. It can be manifest on the skin (Cutaneous Anthrax) in the lungs (Pulmonary / Inhalation Anthrax), and/or intestinal (Gastrointestinal Anthrax and Oropharyngeal anthrax) or CNS (Meningeal Anthrax).", "runs": [{"text": "Anthrax"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bacterial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disease"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "caused"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "spore"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "forming"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Bacillus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "anthraces,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gram"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "positive,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rod-"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "shaped"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bacterium."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a zoonotic disease whereby man is infected directly through contact with infected hides or inhalation of spores in the lungs or ingestion of infected meat. It can be manifest on the skin (Cutaneous Anthrax) in the lungs (Pulmonary / Inhalation Anthrax), and/or intestinal (Gastrointestinal Anthrax and Oropharyngeal anthrax) or CNS (Meningeal Anthrax)."}]}, {"id": "body-03195", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation Cutaneous Anthrax", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation Cutaneous Anthrax"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03196", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Itching, Pruritic papule or vesicle, Characteristic depressed black eschar surrounded by moderate to severe edema, A malignant pustule, Pyrexia.", "runs": [{"text": "Itching, Pruritic papule or vesicle, Characteristic depressed black eschar surrounded by moderate to severe edema, A malignant pustule, Pyrexia."}]}, {"id": "body-03198", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Inhalation Anthrax", "runs": [{"text": "Inhalation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Anthrax"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03199", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Mild inhalation Anthrax", "runs": [{"text": "Mild"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inhalation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Anthrax"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1790"}}, {"id": "body-03200", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Cough, Fever, Fatigue, Myalgia, can resemble a viral respiratory illness, Pulmonary and gastrointestinal signs may occur together", "runs": [{"text": "Cough, Fever, Fatigue, Myalgia, can resemble a viral respiratory illness, Pulmonary and gastrointestinal signs may occur together"}]}, {"id": "body-03201", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Severe inhalation Anthrax", "runs": [{"text": "Severe"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inhalation Anthrax"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1790"}}, {"id": "body-03202", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Diaphoresis, Stridor, Dyspnea, Hypotension, Acute respiratory distress. These patients may develop sepsis accompanied by cyanosis, shock, and hemorrhagic pneumonia. Hemorrhagic pleural effusions often develop.", "runs": [{"text": "Diaphoresis,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Stridor,"}, {"text": " "}, {"tex